# HHX Services — project rules

HHX Services is a Microsoft Power Apps, Dataverse and Power Platform consultancy for small businesses. Site language: **English only**.

## Stack

- Next.js 16 (App Router) + React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS 4
- No framework change, no backend/database yet — this is a Node app, not a static site
- Hosting: Vercel at https://hello-muse.vercel.app/ (GitHub Pages cannot run this Node app)
- Repo: hncrm/Hello-Muse, branch `main`

## Commands

```bash
npm install
npm run dev      # http://localhost:3000
npm run build    # production build — must pass before any push
npm run lint     # ESLint — must pass before any push
npm run test:unit  # Vitest — tests/unit/
npm run test:e2e   # Playwright — tests/e2e/ (needs `npx playwright install`)
```

## Pages (all 7, do not rename routes)

- `/` Home, `/services`, `/about`, `/process`, `/case-studies`, `/blog` (+ `/blog/[slug]`), `/contact`
- Canonical routes are `/case-studies` and `/blog` — not `/testimonials` or `/insights`
- Shared layout/header: `app/layout.tsx`, `components/SiteHeader.tsx`; nav in `lib/nav.ts`

## Hard rules

- **Do not invent clients, results, testimonials, or case studies.** Case studies and blog posts are labelled placeholder/sample until Huy supplies real ones. Replace placeholder content only with real content Huy provides.
- **Do not invent a real contact email.** The placeholder is `hello@hhxservices.example` (see `.env.example` / `CONTACT_NOTIFY_EMAIL`). Huy will confirm the real email later.
- **Do not invent a response time.** The placeholder `[X working days — to be confirmed]` appears in the contact intro, sidebar and confirmation. Leave it until Huy confirms.
- **No email is sent yet.** Enquiries are stored locally in `data/enquiries.json` (git-ignored, interim only). Do not wire up email/Dataverse without Huy's explicit go-ahead.
- Keep the HHX design tokens (Techzo restyle, 2026-11-20; see `app/globals.css`): navy `#010a24`, brand blue `#1267c8`, mid blue `#1492d8`, cyan `#16b9e6`, deep teal `#063642` / `#042b35`; gradient `linear-gradient(90deg, #1267c8, #1492d8, #16b9e6)`; pill buttons; Plus Jakarta Sans; 1290px container; 16px inputs, 48px primary CTA.
- Keep changes small and focused. Run `npm run build`, `npm run lint` and `npm run test:unit` after code changes and fix failures before finishing.
- This repo's Next.js version has breaking changes vs older versions — read the relevant guide in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before writing code that relies on Next.js APIs (see `AGENTS.md`).
